00:07:30,750 --> 00:07:37,150
Next question may be, how can you calculate the consumption of the air in the escaba escuba?

180
00:07:37,150 --> 00:07:42,750
How long will the escaba go? How long can we breathe? How do you know?

181
00:07:42,750 --> 00:07:44,150
So, let's discuss about this.

182
00:07:44,150 --> 00:07:48,950
First of all, the air in the escaba or escuba tank is filled with air.

183
00:07:49,150 --> 00:07:51,150
It is filled with normal air.

184
00:07:51,150 --> 00:07:52,750
It is in your volume.

185
00:07:52,750 --> 00:07:55,150
We call the volume unit cubic feet.

186
00:07:55,150 --> 00:08:02,150
So, for the normal breathing, our air required for 1 minute is 1.5 cubic feet.

187
00:08:02,150 --> 00:08:06,550
When the air is 1.5 cubic feet, we can breathe for a minute.

188
00:08:06,550 --> 00:08:10,350
If we want to breathe for 30 minutes,

189
00:08:10,350 --> 00:08:13,950
then your air should be 45 cubic feet.

190
00:08:13,950 --> 00:08:18,550
So, you can generally calculate it according to 1 minute.

191
00:08:18,750 --> 00:08:21,550
The air in the escaba or escuba is filled with pressure gauge.

192
00:08:21,550 --> 00:08:23,550
You can also find out from there.

193
00:08:23,550 --> 00:08:26,350
If you are showing 100 bars of pressure in the pressure gauge,

194
00:08:26,350 --> 00:08:29,550
then it means you can use it for 15 minutes.

195
00:08:29,550 --> 00:08:33,150
If you are showing 200 bars, then you can use it for 30 minutes.

196
00:08:33,150 --> 00:08:37,150
If you are showing 300 bars, then you can use it for 45 minutes.

197
00:08:37,150 --> 00:08:39,950
So, you can find out like this.

